gap: nvfp4 0.079 vs q4_0 0.0485 -> nvfp4 ~63% worse KLD (gap 0.0306).

## Ceiling (patched N=6 build, force-dequant path)
nvfp4-nosubn:
  Mean PPL(Q)/PPL(base) : 1.020608 +/- 0.001611
  Mean KLD              : 0.040284 +/- 0.001395
  Same top p            : 92.490 +/- 0.117 %

RESULT: nvfp4-nosubn 0.0403 vs baseline nvfp4 0.0791 (-49%) and BEATS q4_0 0.0485 on all 3
metrics (KLD, PPL ratio, top-p), at the same 4.6 bpw. The single global exponent shift (no
per-tensor storage, no new type) more than closes the gap to q4_0.

## N=0 control (standard nvfp4 gguf on force-dequant path = W4A16)
  Mean PPL(Q)/PPL(base) : 1.035339 +/- 0.001857
  Mean KLD              : 0.050030 +/- 0.001504
  Same top p            : 91.482 +/- 0.124 %

=> CONFOUND FOUND: native nvfp4 0.0791 vs dequant nvfp4 0.0500 for the SAME gguf. The 0.029 gap is
the native FP4 path quantizing ACTIVATIONS to fp4 (W4A4) vs the dequant path keeping f16 (W4A16).
Decompose:
  - subnormal rescue (weight format), W4A16: 0.0500 -> 0.0403 = -19% (NOT -49%).
  - activation fp4 (W4A4 vs W4A16): +0.029 KLD (dominant; weight fix can't touch it).
  - "nvfp4-nosubn beats q4_0" was W4A16-vs-W4A8 -> RETRACTED. q4_0-W4A16 pending for fair compare.

